* text=auto eol=lf
model/** -text -eol

# rtl/ takes the default above rather than model/'s verbatim rule, and the difference
# between the two trees is the whole ground. model/ is vendored byte-identically from
# an upstream pin, so any tool that writes CRLF rewrites every line of the file it
# touched and destroys the line counts a curation batch reports as its evidence; -text
# freezes its bytes to protect that evidence. rtl/ holds only files this repository
# authored. There is no upstream to stay identical to and no vendored diff to protect,
# so the same rule would protect nothing while making a normal edit from either lane
# read as a whole-file rewrite. What is stated rather than sniffed is that these
# sources are text: text=auto decides that by inspecting content, and a waveform or a
# generated netlist landing under rtl/ is a thing review should refuse rather than a
# thing an attribute should quietly normalize.
rtl/**/*.sv text eol=lf
